w("- Batch objectives (6.OBJECTIVES&PROBLEM STATEMENT.docx): (1) collect prices + financial news + social media text; (2) preprocess and align into daily instances per trading day; (3) represent each day as a bag of news instances (Multiple Instance Learning); (4) hybrid model: sequence learning over prices + attention over news content; (5) predict directional movement and evaluate with accuracy, precision, recall, F1; (6) compare multi-source against a price-only baseline.")
w("- **What the product does (and does not do) against those objectives - state plainly everywhere:**")
w("  - Obj 1: prices yes (Yahoo Finance, 10 tickers); financial news only as headlines through NewsAPI **when a key is set**, otherwise a labelled synthetic-headline fallback (this run: synthetic for all ten tickers); **no social-media source**.")
w("  - Obj 2: daily alignment yes, but headlines are collapsed to **one mean sentiment number per trading day** (ffill, 0 before the first headline); not a bag.")
w("  - Obj 3: **Multiple Instance Learning is not implemented in QuantPulse.** Attention in the product runs over the 20-day *price* window (multi-head self-attention after the LSTM), not over news instances.")
w("  - Obj 4: LSTM + 4-head attention + sentiment channel + simulated FedAvg ablation: implemented as in the base paper.")
w("  - Obj 5: the product forecasts **price level** (regression: MAE/MSE/RMSE/R2, plus a directional-accuracy figure and an up/down trend flag). **Precision, recall and F1 are not computed by the product.**")
w("  - Obj 6: ablation LSTM -> +attention -> +sentiment -> hybrid exists, but its sentiment channel is synthetic (see 4.2) so it is not a valid multi-source versus price-only comparison.")
w("  - To address objectives 3, 5 and 6 honestly an **offline MIL study with real headlines was added in this documentation run** (`scripts/mil_study.py`, section 4.5). It is not part of the application.\n")

