w("- **Evaluation defect:** test targets pass through `apply_scalers`, which clips to [0,1] of the *training* range; for tickers whose test prices rise above the training maximum the target is flat at the clip bound, so MAE is understated and directional accuracy is inflated (e.g. 0.9 for AAPL: flat target and saturated prediction both read 'not up'). 'True' scoring is in the table above.")
w("- **Sentiment channel is empty during training:** synthetic headlines exist only for the last 90 trading days, so the channel is exactly 0 for every training row (0 non-zero rows in the training part for all ten tickers) and non-zero only in the test part. The sentiment tier is trained on a constant channel and tested on random template values, which is why it is worse than the attention tier and unstable across seeds; a placebo whose sentiment values are shuffled in time (so the channel is non-zero in training too) scores the same as the no-sentiment tier. Either way the ablation cannot show a sentiment effect, positive or negative.")
w("- Federated averaging: two rounds of three local epochs over ten clients starting from one global model; the averaged model is evaluated per ticker on its own scalers although the clients use different price scales (MinMax per ticker). It scores worse than the local tiers.\n")

